[[File:1962 Tour de France map.png|thumb|350px|Route of the [[1962 Tour de France]]; followed counterclockwise, starting in [[Nancy, France|Nancy]] and finishing in Paris]]
The [[1962 Tour de France]] was the 49th edition of the Tour de France, one of cycling's [[Grand Tour (cycling)|Grand Tours]]. It took place between from 24 June and 15 July, with 22 stages covering a distance of {{convert|4274|km|0|abbr=on}}. After more than 30 years, the Tour was again contested by trade teams. Frenchman [[Jacques Anquetil]] defended his title, winning his third Tour de France.<ref name="bri-1962">{{cite web|title=1962 Tour de France|url=http://bikeraceinfo.com/tdf/tdf1962.html|access-date=4 October 2016|work=BikeRaceInfo|publisher=McGann Publishing|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161111003512/http://bikeraceinfo.com/tdf/tdf1962.html|archive-date=11 November 2016|url-status=live}}</ref>

